From b6d6c53288bc5b7e3869569641c43ab0cce7b418 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:06:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] feat(auth): hermes auth disable/enable keeps a
 pooled credential from being used

User-disabled accounts live in auth.json disabled_credentials (provider -> [{id,label}]),
never on pool rows, so stale pool writers (rotation, refresh, hub pulls) cannot undo a
disable. Matching by id or case-insensitive label keeps a re-created row (re-login, hub
pull) disabled. The active store's section is unioned with the global root's; reads are
cached by (mtime, size) so a disable from another process reaches live pools on their next
selection.

- _available_entries skips disabled rows: select, peek, reclaim, has_available and
  rotation never return one; all-disabled = no available entry.
- token_is_blocked treats a disabled account's token as blocked for every model, closing
  the env/borrowed Anthropic paths that bypass selection.
- pinned_anthropic_pool_token reports a disabled pinned entry as gone, so a live session
  rebinds to an enabled account on its next pre-request check.
- CLI: hermes auth disable|enable <provider> <target>; auth list tags [disabled].

Proof: tests/agent/test_credential_pool_disabled.py (15) RED on main (14 fail), GREEN here;
tests/hermes_cli/test_auth_disable_command.py; 933 pool/anthropic/routing/auth tests green;
scripts/check ok.
